%description:

Tcp.dupthresh:rfc5681-rack -- the fast retransmission follows the third duplicate ACK.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the duplicate ACK threshold of the fast retransmit (RFC 5681, RFC 6675)
...; with RACK, the number of SACKed segments at which the reordering window becomes 0".

The classes: rfc5681 (3, the default, the value of RFC 5681 and RFC 6675), other (another
count), invalid (0 and less). Each class has two facets: the loss detection "rack", the
default, and "dupthresh". The code: with "dupthresh", the fast retransmit comes at DupThresh
duplicate ACKs, or when IsLost() counts DupThresh SACKed segments
(Rfc6675Recovery::receivedDuplicateAck()); with "rack", the reordering window becomes 0 when
DupThresh segments are SACKed and no reordering was seen, so RACK marks the hole lost at once
(Rfc6675Recovery::rackDetectAndMarkLost()). TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks
the value. This test separates "rfc5681" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with RACK, the default loss detection, which sends 500000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 100th data
segment once, where the window holds more than 5 segments after it. Observation: level 1, when
host1 retransmits the 100th segment, it has received 3 ACKs that acknowledge the data up to
the segment and SACK data above it: the duplicate ACKs of RFC 6675, which counts an ACK with
new SACK information. An ACK whose header is longer than 32 bytes has a SACK option.

%# parameter: Tcp.dupthresh
%# class: rfc5681-rack
%# value: 3
%# key: *.host1.tcp.dupthresh
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDupthreshRfc5681Rack")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 143352 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 100th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 143352 && tcp.headerLength > 32B")
                                        .captureCount("dupacks")
                                        .within(5.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 143352 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the 100th data segment of host1")
             .within(2.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 143352 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{dupacks} == 3")
             .describe("the retransmission of the 100th segment")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDupthreshRfc5681Rack compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.dupthresh = 3    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 500000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDupthreshRfc5681Rack: PASS
